<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7378" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">censītĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		1. censeo, censītus. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A taxing</i>, <i>tax</i>, <i>tribute</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">levare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Spart. Pescenn. Nigr. 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A declaration of the will</i>, <i>a
				command</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vespasiani censitione et jussu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Colon. p. 146</span></i>
			 Goes.</div>
